<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amazon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Amazon rainforest</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Amazon is the vast rainforest and river basin of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, most of which lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> it remained a sparsely settled frontier region, and the government sought to assert control over its territory and river trade. Later in the nineteenth century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> trade brought new economic importance to the region.</p></div>
